// Crop groups: where each grew wild on the real Earth, and the climate it tolerates.
//
// Each climate range is four numbers: below the first the crop cannot grow, from the second to
// the third it grows at its best, and above the fourth it cannot grow; in between, how well it
// grows rises or falls in a straight line.
//   warmest  mean temperature of the warmest month, degrees C
//   coldest  mean temperature of the coldest month, degrees C
//   water    rainfall over the year plus what a river adds (see farming.json), mm
// Every crop needs a warmest month of at least 10 degrees C, so none grows in tundra or ice.
// The homeland is a circle on the real Earth: cells inside it where the crop grows well at the
// start of a run are where it grows wild and can first be farmed. An inventionFactor (1 unless
// given) makes a crop that much likelier to be first farmed than farming.json's inventionChance:
// wheat and barley's wild lands are small, and without it they were first farmed anywhere from
// 9950 to 5650 BCE across seeds (on Earth about 9500 BCE, before any other crop).
